# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending-normalised or diffed as text.
#
# Git guesses text-vs-binary from content, and a SQLite file is mostly bytes that
# look like nothing — but "mostly" is not a guarantee, and a single CRLF
# translation inside a frozen state dir would corrupt a fixture whose entire
# value is being byte-for-byte what a released binary wrote. Declaring it removes
# the guess.
#
# `diff` is set so `git diff` reports "Binary files differ" instead of dumping
# kilobytes of noise into a review.
*.db     binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary
*.bak    binary
*.kxjournal binary
*.fds    binary
*.gguf   binary
